WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.420
Ride on consecutive days and your streak grows. The backend keeps it, so every

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:08.589
screen agrees.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.164
Each calendar day with a finished ride adds one, in your own time zone. A second

00:00:15.164 --> 00:00:19.941
ride that day doesn't count twice. Miss a whole day and it's back to zero.

00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:31.041
The streak pays: ten XP a day on every ride, in the same number the header shows.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.364
The flame and the count sit in the header, and Profile reads seven hundred sixty XP

00:00:41.364 --> 00:00:45.005
to level eight, four-day streak. No streak, no flame.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.537
What the tests prove: every case of the rule, the streak through the API across

00:00:53.537 --> 00:00:55.944
midnight, and the header and Profile.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:03.965
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:08.821
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:08.821 --> 00:01:10.492
every hill and interval.

00:01:10.838 --> 00:01:16.016
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:16.016 --> 00:01:21.464
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:21.464 --> 00:01:24.454
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:27.291
A custom workout lives under Profile.
